From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: gs101-pixel: keep the GNSS LDOs on

The BCM4775 GNSS receiver on spi10 is fed by s2mpg11 ldo9s (core),
ldo10s (RF) and ldo11s (aux). Nothing claims them, so the regulator core
switches them off at late init and the receiver never answers MCU_REQ.
The stock device tree marks all three regulator-always-on (the vendor
driver has no regulator handling and parks the chip with nstandby);
do the same. With them on, MCU_RESP rises as soon as nstandby is
released.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-pixel-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-pixel-common.dtsi
@@ -1059,18 +1059,21 @@
 				regulator-name = "vdd_gnss";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <725000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1300000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
 			ldo10s {
 				regulator-name = "vdd_gnss_rf";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <1600000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1950000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
 			ldo11s {
 				regulator-name = "vdd_gnss_aux";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <1600000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1950000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
 			/* ldo12s is unused */
